# MATSEL PRO — API Documentation

MATSEL PRO uses a Flask backend to connect the frontend with the material database, recommendation logic, cost model, manufacturing information and AI services.

## Architecture

```text
Frontend
   ↓
HTTP / JSON
   ↓
Flask Backend
   ↓
Processing & Recommendation Logic
   ↓
Database / AI Layer
```

## Core API Functions

### Material Recommendation

Accepts product and application requirements and returns ranked material candidates.

Typical inputs include:

```text
Product Line
Sub-category
Application
Target Budget
Production Volume
```

Processing flow:

```text
User Input
   ↓
Application Context
   ↓
Dynamic Weights
   ↓
Database Filtering
   ↓
Multi-Criteria Scoring
   ↓
Ranked Materials
```

### Manufacturing Process

Maps a selected material to compatible manufacturing processes and surface-finishing options.

### Cost Estimation

Calculates estimated unit cost based on:

```text
Material Cost
+
Manufacturing Cost
+
Surface Treatment
+
Tooling
+
Overhead
```

### Image Intelligence

Accepts a product image and performs AI-based analysis to identify:

* Product characteristics
* Material family
* Surface finish
* Aesthetic intent
* Visual properties
* Engineering observations

The resulting information is used for material and manufacturing recommendations.

